{{!-- BUILDS

      Only appears once a build has been dragged here from the builder's rail.
      An empty strip would be a permanent question about a feature most
      characters never use.

      Clicking one EQUIPS it, which is the whole point of a build being on the
      handle: switching kit without opening anything. It confirms first, like
      every other path to applying does. --}}
{{#if (getHandleBuilds actor)}}
<div class="handle-builds">
    {{#each (getHandleBuilds actor)}}
        <div draggable="true"
             class="squire-handle-control handle-build-icon"
             data-build-id="{{this.id}}"
             data-tooltip="<strong>{{this.name}}</strong><br>{{#if this.costume}}Costume &mdash; changes the portrait and token only<br><em>Click to wear</em>{{else}}AC {{this.armorClass}} · {{this.gearCount}} items<br><em>Click to equip</em>{{/if}}<br><em>Right-click to take off the handle</em>">
            {{#if this.img}}
            <img draggable="false" src="{{this.img}}" alt="{{this.name}}"/>
            {{else}}
            <i class="fa-solid {{#if this.costume}}fa-masks-theater{{else}}fa-shirt{{/if}} handle-build-blank"></i>
            {{/if}}
            {{!-- The same two glyphs the rail's tiles and the New buttons use, so
                  one mark means one kind of thing wherever it appears. It was
                  the runner on everything, which named the ACTION rather than
                  the thing — and named it wrongly on a costume, which is worn
                  rather than equipped. --}}
            <i class="fa-solid {{#if this.costume}}fa-masks-theater{{else}}fa-shirt{{/if}} handle-build-overlay"></i>
        </div>
    {{/each}}
</div>
{{/if}}

{{!-- WHAT THE WORN BUILD PUTS ON THE HANDLE

      Derived from whichever build is currently worn, never stored — a second
      list would go stale the moment somebody edited the build it was copied
      from. Its own zone, separate from the favourites below, because those were
      dragged there by hand and a build must never remove them: without the
      separation, applying a build would have to guess which icons were its to
      take, and the only honest answer to "who put this here" is to have
      recorded it.

      THREE, and which three depends on the character: a martial gets Main Hand,
      Both Hands and Off Hand, a caster gets their Primary, Secondary and
      Tertiary spells. Those are the same three big slots the doll gives them, so
      the handle shows whatever that character's build is actually built around
      rather than a fixed idea of what a build is for. --}}
{{#if (getHandleBuildActions actor)}}
<div class="handle-build-weapons">
    {{#each (getHandleBuildActions actor)}}
        <div class="squire-handle-control handle-favorite-icon handle-build-weapon"
             data-item-id="{{this.id}}"
             data-tooltip="<strong>{{this.name}}</strong><br><em>From the build you are wearing</em>">
            <img draggable="false" src="{{this.img}}" alt="{{this.name}}"/>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-dice-d20 squire-roll-overlay handle-favorite-roll-overlay"></i>
        </div>
    {{/each}}
</div>
{{/if}}
